				\begin{document}$$CK or = \frac{{P_{O} - P_{E} }}{{1 - P_{E} }}$$\end{document}CKor=PO-PE1-PEwhere true positive (TP) is the number of true hemolytic peptides that are predicted correctly; true negative (TN) is the number of true non-hemolytic peptides that are predicted correctly; false positive (FP) is the number of true hemolytic peptides that are predicted to be non-hemolytic; true negative (TN) is the number of true non-hemolytic peptides that are predicted to be hemolytic; PO is the relative observed agreement among raters and PE is the hypothetical probability of chance agreement.Table 1
